  "stem": "A water tank holds 640 liters of water at time \\(t = 0\\) hours. The number of liters remaining \\(t\\) hours later is modeled by \\(V(t) = 640\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{t/3}\\). After how many hours will 20 liters remain?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "15"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set the model equal to \\(20\\): \\(640\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{t/3} = 20\\).",
    "Divide by \\(640\\): \\(\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^{t/3} = \\dfrac{1}{32}\\), since \\(\\dfrac{20}{640} = \\dfrac{1}{32}\\).",
    "Because \\(32 = 2^{5}\\), \\(\\dfrac{t}{3} = 5\\), so \\(t = 15\\)."
  ],
  "verify": "t = symbols('t')\nV = 640*Rational(1, 2)**(t/3)\nassert simplify(V.subs(t, 15)) == 20\nassert [simplify(s) for s in solve(Eq(V, 20), t)] == [15]\nassert spr_answers == ['15']",
